        1769,
        1491,
        2017
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "\u00a7 3. Where the provisions of the 1968 Building Code apply to the alteration of a prior code building in accordance with section 28-101.4.3 of the Administrative Code of the City of New York, I hereby suspend section 27-359, and the corresponding capacity requirements in table 6-1 of article 2 of subchapter 6 of chapter 1 of title 27, of the Administrative Code of the City of New York, to the extent that they would prevent the alteration and/or use of buildings as temporary humanitarian relief centers (\"Humanitarian Emergency Response and Relief Centers\")",
